#~ msgid ""
#~ "The **Watcher** window shows the "
#~ "registers and some places in memory, "
#~ "and follows them while the machine "
#~ "runs. Open it with **Debug > "
#~ "Watcher** in the main window, or "
#~ "**Watcher** under the **Tools** button "
#~ "over the listing."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Expression** - an address, in the "
#~ "same syntax as a condition (see "
#~ "[Conditions](#conditions)): `HL`, `0x5C3A`, `IX "
#~ "+ 5`, `[0x5C53]`, a label. The "
#~ "button beside it opens the list of"
#~ " labels; a label picked there goes"
#~ " into the field."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**OK** takes it only when the "
#~ "expression is right. The first row "
#~ "of a watch shows its type and "
#~ "expression, and its value as an "
#~ "address; the second row the 13 "
#~ "bytes that start at that address. "
#~ "`??` means the expression cannot be "
#~ "worked out at the moment."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "In the **Breakpoints** panel, press add"
#~ " (the plus sign). The editor opens"
#~ " on a **CPU address** with **Fetch**"
#~ " ticked."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid "Press **OK** and close the Debugger."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid "In the **Breakpoints** panel, press add."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Select the new row in the "
#~ "**Breakpoints** panel and press edit "
#~ "(the pencil)."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Set **Action** to **Counter** and tick"
#~ " **Log**. To log only some values,"
#~ " type them into the field beside "
#~ "it, such as `A, HL, M(HL)`. Press"
#~ " **OK**."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid "Select the new row in the **Breakpoints** panel and press edit."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "In the **Breakpoints** panel, press add."
#~ " Type `START` into **Address**; the "
#~ "line under it says `8000, START`. "
#~ "Set **Span** to **Opens a span** "
#~ "and **Action** to **Counter**. Press "
#~ "**OK**."
#~ msgstr ""

